Cursor [SimTalk]
Sets the cell in the list with one column designated by <Path> in which the cursor is placed.
Remarks
The attribute applies to the DataList, the DataStack, and the DataQueue.
All methods that use ranges, such as find or max, use the current position of the cursor. Plant Simulation
ignores ranges located before the current cursor position. The method starts its task beginning at the
cursor position. If a method does not return the expected values, check the cursor position.
Note
You can also set the cursor by using a user-defined index. Use the method setCursor when using a
user-defined index of data type integer.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Cursor:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
MyDataStack.Cursor := 1
MyDataQueue.Cursor := 2
MyDataList.Cursor := MyDataList.Cursor + 1
